[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat-V weir. Catchment highly urbanised and industrialised. GENERAL: Flat-V weir, 5m wide (1:10 cross-slope) in steep-sided, straight channel. No cableway. May be subject to accretion and bank encroachment but well maintained and should not affect high flow ratings. STATION HYDROMETRY: High concrete wing-walls prevent bypassing. Substantial modular range, drops away quickly over a cascade of weirs downstream of the gauge. Downstream level recorder suggests station remains modular in all events. One peak flow rating applied across period of record. Theoretical rating with current meter check gaugings from bridge. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Stormwater drainage in part of the catchment but very few abstractions or discharges. An outfall draining a large urban area joins the beck just downstream of the station.
CATCHMENT,A small, relatively low-lying impervious (Coal Measures) catchment with significant urban/suburban development on the periphery of Leeds. Catchment is traversed by both the M1 and M62. Increasing urbanisation during period of record.
Qmed Suitability,Not gauged to within 30% of QMED. However, structure is to British standard and theoretical rating is thought to be reliable.
Pooling Suitability,British standard weir with downstream recorder; not bypassed.
[END]
